  "final_answer": "I have all the information needed. Let me provide the detailed route information from Miami to New Orleans.\n\n## Route from Miami to New Orleans 🚗\n\n### Starting Point: Miami, Florida, USA (迈阿密 美国佛罗里达州)\n### Destination: New Orleans, Louisiana, USA (新奥尔良 美国路易斯安那州)\n\n---\n\n### 🛣️ Available Travel Modes\n\n| Mode | Duration |\n|------|----------|\n| 🚗 Driving | **12 hours 18 minutes** |\n| 🚌 Public Transit | 1 day |\n| 🚶 Walking | 14 days |\n| 🚴 Cycling | 4 days |\n| ✈️ Flight | 2 hours |\n\n---\n\n### 🚗 Best Driving Route (Currently Selected)\n\n- **Duration:** 12 hours 18 minutes\n- **Distance:** 878 miles (约 1,413 km)\n- **Main Highway:** I-10 W (Interstate 10 West)\n- **Highlights:** Currently the fastest route, avoids road closures on Florida's Turnpike\n- **⚠️ Warnings:**\n  - This route includes tolls (此路线有收费站)\n  - Destination is in a different time zone (your destination is in a different time zone)\n\n---\n\n### 🚗 Alternative Driving Route\n\n- **Duration:** 12 hours 31 minutes\n- **Distance:** 896 miles (约 1,442 km)\n- **Main Highways:** I-95 N and I-10 W\n- **Highlights:** Avoids road closures on Florida's Turnpike\n\n---\n\n### ✈️ Flight Option\n\n- **Duration:** 2 hours (flight time)\n- **Route:** Fort Lauderdale, USA → New Orleans, USA\n\n---\n\n### 📍 Summary\n\nThe **recommended route** is the **driving route via I-10 W**, which covers **878 miles** in approximately **12 hours 18 minutes**. This route is faster and avoids road closures on Florida's Turnpike, though it does include some tolls. The route passes through the southeastern United States and crosses into a different time zone upon arrival in New Orleans.\n\nNote: I was unable to view the detailed turn-by-turn directions as the overlay covered them, but the summary information above represents the most important route details shown on Google Maps.",
